or  housing healthcare for  example the amounts are important  but we also need to know that speed  really matters at the moment being  and the money is needed now  and this is the reason why we're making  sure that 3.4 billion euros  of this bigger package of 17 billion  will be front loaded so to give  immediately liquidity to the member  states that are hosting refugees  we also support those in ukraine who so  bravely resist the kremlin's forces  ramped up our support to ukraine with 1  billion from the eu budget for military  assistance  and many eu members are delivering such  assistance on a bilateral basis  on top of this we have presented  measures to support food security and  agriculture in ukraine  because putin's war is starting to have  a serious impact on food security in  ukraine and globally  ukraine and russia together account for  one-third  of the world's wheat exports  therefore we must avoid a global food  crisis and we have to act now  we are providing  24.5 billion euros until 2024  to help the regions most affected by  food insecurity  third and finally on breaking free from  russia's fossil fuels  this morning president biden and i  agreed on an unprecedented partnership  to reduce europe's dependency on russian  gas  and in parallel  we agreed on this partnership to really  accelerate the green transition  as a first step the united states will  provide us with an additional  at least 15 billion cubic meter of lng  this year  in other words this replaces the amount  of russian lng for this year  and in the coming years  we're aiming for at least 50 billion  cubic meters per year  and this would be able to replace one  third of all russian gas supply to  europe  this is significant  and on top our investment will also pave  the way for the deployment of green  energy because the infrastructure  that we use for gas today and that we  are investing in  can also be used for clean hydrogen in  the future  this agreement with the united states  